@nsobid-6830B3A12406CB4716FEC5ADDC35D3E2DC92D212

# Splatoon 3 11.2.0 - 2560x1440 resolution

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Renders at 2560x1440 instead of the stock docked 1080p.
//
// Three sizes have to move together: the sead physical framebuffer (the NVN
// window texture, which sets the ceiling), the render size at gfxstate+0x388
// (what the render targets are actually allocated at), and the crop rectangle
// handed to nvnWindowSetCrop. Move only the first and you get a 2560x1440
// window showing an upscaled 1080p image.
//
// REQUIRES Ryujinx > System > DRAM Size set to 8 GiB or 12 GiB. The agl
// dynamic-texture pool is a fixed 128 MB that does not scale with resolution,
// so it is raised to 512 MB here -- which overshoots a budget the engine
// asserts on, so that assertion is bypassed too.
//
// Use DOCKED mode (System > "Enable Docked Mode"); handheld sizes are stock.

@enabled
// sead physical framebuffer / NVN window textures, built as two immediates in
// nnMain's sead::GameFrameworkNx::CreateArg.
0442EAF4 0AB48052   // MOVZ W10,#1440        (was 1080)
0442EB1C 0840C1F2   // MOVK X8,#2560,LSL#32  (was 1920)
// Make the dynamic-resolution controller's apply path run on the first frame
// and publish this size to gfxstate+0x388, the field render targets are sized
// from. It normally fires only on an operation-mode change, which never happens
// when you boot straight into docked mode.
013638AC 08008052   // MOVZ W8,#0     (ctrl+0x320 cached op mode; was 1)
01363AE0 09B48052   // MOVZ W9,#1440  (was ladder[idx])
01363B34 0A408152   // MOVZ W10,#2560 (was FCVTZS W10,S0 = height/9*16)
// Drop that path's display-buffer crop write -- the display buffer does not
// exist yet on frame 1. The per-frame path below repeats it behind a null guard.
01363B44 1F2003D5   // NOP (was LDR  X11,[X11,#0x50]  = display buffer)
01363B48 1F2003D5   // NOP (was STRB W12,[X11,#0x52]  = crop dirty)
01363B4C 1F2003D5   // NOP (was STUR XZR,[X11,#0x54]  = crop x,y)
01363B50 1F2003D5   // NOP (was STP  W10,W9,[X11,#0x5C] = crop w,h)
// Force the controller's full-resolution flag (ctrl+0x31C) at both read sites,
// bypassing its per-frame min(ladder/height, 1.0) shrink.
01363B54 29008052   // MOVZ W9,#1
01363C08 2C008052   // MOVZ W12,#1
// Pin the two loads that feed nvnWindowSetCrop to the same size.
01363BFC 0A408152   // MOVZ W10,#2560 (was LDR W10,[X11,#0x388])
01363C04 09B48052   // MOVZ W9,#1440  (was LDR W9,[X11,#0x38C])
// Enlarge the fixed agl dynamic-texture pool to 512 MB. sub_710135AE88 looks
// it up by name and falls back to a hardcoded 128 MB; both arms of the CSEL need
// patching, since the config value wins when present. This mod OWNS these four
// offsets -- do not duplicate them in another enabled mod.
0135AF04 0900A452   // MOVZ W9,#0x2000,LSL#16  (config value)
0135AF0C 0800A452   // MOVZ W8,#0x2000,LSL#16  (default; was 0x800 = 128 MB)
0135AF4C 1500A452   // MOVZ W21,#0x2000,LSL#16 (null-config fallback)
0135AF58 1500A452   // MOVZ W21,#0x2000,LSL#16 (null-config fallback)
// sead's heap arrangement halts if a heap exceeds its planned budget -- but it
// checks AFTER creating the heap, so the memory was obtained successfully and
// this is only bookkeeping. Redirect the halt past the check; it cannot be NOPed
// because the halt is noreturn and the next word is the following function.
04DA16B0 EAFFFF17   // B loc_7104DA1658 (was BL sub_7104521E30 = halt)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Splatoon 3's sead + spl::gfx + agl/gsys
// engine; 11.2.0 retail is symbol-stripped, so every site was located by
// structure and byte-verified against the IDB.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
